WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.586
01  Prepare an agent request
The request stays unsent. The next steps demonstrate manual circuit editing.

00:00:14.586 --> 00:00:26.742
02  Open main.tsx in T3’s default editor
Use Ctrl P to find the circuit source. The normal file tree and editor are preserved.

00:00:26.742 --> 00:00:35.110
03  Change the resistor from 330 ohms to 1k
Edit the real TSX file, then save it with Ctrl S.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:47.599
04  Build the circuit in T3’s terminal
Run the standard tscircuit build. Read both the result and the part warnings.

00:00:47.599 --> 00:01:00.600
05  Inspect the standard tscircuit preview
The existing Browser panel displays tsci dev. R1 now reads 1kΩ.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:14.269
06  Review the exact source change
Use git diff in the normal terminal before you commit your circuit changes.

00:01:14.269 --> 00:01:29.086
07  Export fabrication files with the CLI
The starter needs engineering and part review before manufacturing.

00:01:29.086 --> 00:01:36.758
TSCI Code · Circuit workflow complete
T3’s original editor, terminal, and Browser. Your project remains a normal Git repository.
